<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Historical Sites – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Historical Sites and Tourism</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Our Historical Sites</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write simple texts giving key information about oneself and one's culture. Interactive: Edit narrative texts written by peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a simple text sharing a personal cultural tradition (e.g., "Describe your family's celebration of Carnival and explain a key tradition, such as attending parades or dancing at the culcos."). Can edit a peer's narrative on Indigenous traditions by suggesting additional details (e.g., "I think you can add more details about the colors in traditional clothing."). Can edit a peer's descriptive paragraph on a festival (e.g., "You could add some adjectives like 'colorful' or 'exciting' to make it sound more vivid and fun.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays images of three famous Panamanian historical sites (e.g., Casco Viejo, Panama Canal, Panama Viejo ruins) on the board. Students are asked to quickly write down one adjective and one noun for each site that describes it. (e.g., "Casco Viejo: old, architecture"; "Panama Canal: famous, transit"). This activates prior vocabulary and sets the writing focus.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to describe a picture of a historical site using two simple sentences, writing them on the board. For example, pointing to Casco Viejo: "Casco Viejo is a cultural heritage site. It has beautiful colonial architecture." The teacher emphasizes using clear, descriptive language and the correct present simple tense. The teacher also models the stress in words like "culture" and "cultural."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What kind of words do we use to describe how a place looks or feels?" (Expected answer: Adjectives).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If something happened many years ago, what verb tense do we use?" (Expected answer: Simple past).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Historical Sites and Tourism".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short descriptive paragraph (approx. 70-80 words) from a tourist brochure or travel blog entry about "Portobelo: A Historical Gem." The text incorporates target vocabulary (e.g., ruins, port, fort, colony, attract, explore, ancient, preserved, famous) and grammar (present simple, simple past, possessive 's).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Example Text:</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"Portobelo, located on Panama's Caribbean coast, is a truly historical site. This ancient port was a significant colony for the Spanish in the past. Today, visitors can explore the impressive ruins of its old forts, like San Jerónimo and Santiago de la Gloria. Portobelo's rich heritage attracts many tourists who want to learn about its strategic importance. The town is famous for its preserved architecture and offers an informative tour into Panama's colonial history. Many people are going to visit Portobelo next year!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Understanding descriptive texts that provide information about historical sites and their importance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the text individually.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is the main purpose of this text?" (Expected answer: To describe Portobelo and its historical importance for tourists).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students answer T/F questions based on the text (e.g., "Portobelo was important for the French in the past." F; "Visitors can see old forts in Portobelo." T).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Matching:</b> Students match bolded vocabulary words from the text (e.g., <i>ruins, heritage, attract, ancient</i>) with simple definitions or synonyms provided by the teacher.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Present simple and simple past for describing places and their importance; future tense with "going to" for plans; possessive forms with 's.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> historical sites, ruins, Panama Canal, Casco Viejo, landmarks, architecture, heritage, monument, destination, visitor, museum, tour, Causeway, colony, port, fort; attract, visit, guide, find, explore, travel, preserve, describe, inform; historical, cultural, famous, ancient, preserved, tourist-friendly, informative, renowned.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic:</b> Understanding intent and context for informative descriptions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Focus on stress in multisyllabic words used (e.g., "culture," "cultural," "history," "historical," "inform," and "information").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice (Sentence Building):</b> Students complete sentences about Panamanian historical sites using target vocabulary and the correct tense (present simple or simple past). For example: "Casco Viejo _______ (be) a vibrant colonial village." "Many tourists _______ (attract) to Panama's historical sites." "Visitors _______ (be going to visit) the Panama Canal next month."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice (Guided Description):</b> The teacher provides prompts for students to write 2-3 sentences each, describing specific aspects of a chosen historical site. Students must use at least one adjective and one verb from the target list. For example: "Describe the architecture of Casco Viejo." (e.g., "Casco Viejo's architecture is preserved. It has narrow, historical streets."). "Explain what the Panama Canal is known for." (e.g., "The Panama Canal is a famous landmark. It allows ships to transit between two oceans."). Students practice writing sentences with correct possessive 's and descriptive adjectives like 'colorful' or 'exciting'.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction / Peer Check (Sentence Editing):</b> In pairs, students exchange their sentences from the previous activity. They check their partner's sentences for correct use of present simple/simple past and proper use of possessive 's. They offer suggestions for adding more vivid adjectives (e.g., "You could add some adjectives like 'colorful' or 'exciting' to make it sound more vivid and fun.") or improving clarity. Teacher monitors and provides assistance, highlighting stress in multisyllabic words if students read their sentences aloud.</li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Historical Sites and Tourism".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Task:</b> "Write a Tourist Guide Entry."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will individually write a short descriptive paragraph (60-80 words) for a tourist brochure or website about a Panamanian historical site (e.g., Casco Viejo, Panama Canal, Panama Viejo, Portobelo, or a local historical landmark). They must provide key information, describe its importance, and suggest what visitors can do or see there. Alternatively, students can choose to write a simple text sharing a personal cultural tradition as per the learning outcome.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Instructions:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Choose ONE Panamanian historical site or a personal cultural tradition.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Write a paragraph (60-80 words) describing it for a tourist or someone learning about your culture.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include at least three vocabulary words from our list (e.g., <i>landmarks, heritage, explore, historical, preserved, destination</i>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use present simple to describe current facts, simple past for historical facts, and "going to" for future activities or plans.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ensure your text has an informative tone.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Action:</b> The teacher circulates, offering guidance, checking for appropriate vocabulary and grammar use, and encouraging students to use descriptive adjectives to make their writing more engaging. Teacher reminds students to consider the "informative" tone for their article.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Peer Editing and Revision.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students exchange their "Tourist Guide Entry" paragraphs with a partner. Each student uses a simple checklist to provide feedback and suggest improvements for their peer's writing. This directly addresses the learning outcome: "Can edit a peer's descriptive paragraph on a festival (e.g., 'You could add some adjectives like 'colorful' or 'exciting' to make it sound more vivid and fun.')" and "Can edit a peer's narrative on Indigenous traditions by suggesting additional details."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Peer Editing Checklist:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is the main idea clear? Yes / No</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are at least 3 target vocabulary words used correctly? Yes / No (Circle them).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are present simple, simple past, or "going to" used correctly? Yes / No</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are there any possessive 's forms used correctly? Yes / No</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Suggestion for additional details/adjectives (e.g., "I think you can add more details about the colors in traditional clothing." or "You could add an adjective like 'beautiful' or 'fascinating' here.")</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After peer feedback, students revise their own paragraphs based on the suggestions. The teacher collects the original and revised texts for formative assessment.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher's observation of final revised text):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of the descriptive text.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (at least 3-4 words).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct application of present simple, simple past, and "going to."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effort in revision based on peer feedback.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following prompts on a slip of paper:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I learned about writing descriptions today is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One suggestion my partner gave me that helped improve my writing was..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing the tourist guide entry was most challenging for you, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did using the specific vocabulary words (e.g., 'preserved,' 'attract,' 'heritage') help make your writing more informative?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., peer editing was effective, students used target vocabulary creatively).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students' writing development in the next lesson? (e.g., more practice with complex sentence structures, reviewing common errors in simple past).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> The writing and editing skills practiced today will be crucial for Lesson 5, where students will consolidate information about historical sites and possibly contribute to a class project (e.g., creating a digital tourist brochure or a short presentation) that requires clear, well-structured written output.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>